    "narrative": "The Austin Waves are primed for a high-ceiling day, headlined by **Gunnar Henderson** (83.29) and **Kyle Tucker** (76.68). **Gunnar Henderson** remains our most potent asset, benefiting from a substantial 16% park boost against Warren that easily offsets his negative SP skill rating. His leadoff spot in the order guarantees volume, while **Kyle Tucker** occupies the clean-up role against Houser, maximizing his base projection with a strong SP matchup. **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (74.56) and **Jackson Merrill** (72.30) also emerge as must-starts; both are seeing significant efficiency gains from dynamic platoon advantages against right-handed starters, with **Jackson Merrill** providing additional value as a primary source of stolen bases despite the risk posed by an elite hold pitcher.\n\nThe most difficult roster decision today involves the utility slot and our bench depth. **Nolan Schanuel** (60.12) ultimately secured the start over **Josh Jung** (56.92) due to a superior matchup against Cecconi. While **Josh Jung** projects well, the difficulty of facing Gallen necessitated a more conservative approach to preserve game caps. Similarly, **Miguel Vargas** was sidelined despite a decent score, as the combination of a park penalty and concerns regarding base-stealing opportunities against Kolek made him a suboptimal pivot compared to our active outfielders.\n\nWe are monitoring several situational risks closely. While **Josh Lowe** (63.35) remains in the lineup for his elite sprint speed, his score is tempered by the presence of a strong arm behind the plate, limiting his upside on the basepaths. Conversely, **Liam Hicks** (59.93) is a marginal play that warrants a closer look as the day progresses; should his lineup position drop, we may look to consolidate our defensive caps. We are proceeding with the current configuration, banking on the high-floor production of **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (73.08) to anchor the middle of the order and maintain our competitiveness in batting average.",
